Library-strandedness basis
- Lexogen QuantSeq FWD official documentation says the protocol is strand-specific, generates one fragment close to the transcript 3-prime end, and Read 1 directly reflects the mRNA sequence. The FWD orientation therefore supports featureCounts -s 1 (same-strand counting); -s 0 and -s 2 were retained as empirical controls.

featureCounts tests
- Common parameters: featureCounts -T 4 -a GTF -t exon -g gene_id BAM; single-end mode; multimapping and multi-overlap reads not counted.
- -s 0: Assigned 2,747,326 (26.8% of 10,246,567 alignments); Unassigned_NoFeatures 2,000,029; Unassigned_Ambiguity 252,691; Unassigned_Unmapped 1,809,023; detected genes 21,020.
- -s 1: Assigned 2,888,097 (28.2%); Unassigned_NoFeatures 2,038,734; Unassigned_Ambiguity 73,215; Unassigned_Unmapped 1,809,023; detected genes 19,482.
- -s 2: Assigned 214,016 (2.1%); Unassigned_NoFeatures 4,779,994; Unassigned_Ambiguity 6,036; Unassigned_Unmapped 1,809,023; detected genes 7,404.
- Recommended setting for this QuantSeq FWD test: featureCounts -s 1. This is supported by the library chemistry and the strong reduction in ambiguity versus -s 0; -s 2 is clearly incompatible. The highest assigned fraction alone was not used as the criterion.

